.\" coscad(1) - CoScad compiler manual page (mdoc)
.Dd September 11, 2026
.Dt COSCAD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm coscad
.Nd glyph/pipeline CAD language compiler: .coscad and .assemble to OpenSCAD, STL, and print beds
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar part.coscad
.Op Fl o Ar part.scad
.Nm
.Cm stl
.Ar part.coscad
.Op Fl o Ar part.stl
.Nm
.Ar spec.assemble
.Nm
.Cm next
.Ar spec.assemble
.Nm
.Cm check
.Ar spec.assemble
.Op Fl -keep-temp
.Nm
.Cm doctor
.Nm
.Fl -version | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compiles CoScad part files to OpenSCAD source and, with OpenSCAD and the
BOSL2 library installed, renders them to STL.
A
.Pa .coscad
file is a list of definitions, one per line; the definition named
.Ql main
is the rendered shape.
An
.Pa .assemble
file declares physically separate parts, how many to print, and how they
sit together; the manufacturing stage orients and packs them onto print
beds.
.Pp
Anchors, attachments, bezier outlines, lofts, fit checks, print orientation,
and bed packing are all computed in the compiler, so the emitted OpenSCAD
stays plain
.Pq translate , rotate , union , difference , BOSL2 primitives
and any expression, including composites, can be attached to again.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm Ar part.coscad Op Fl o Ar out.scad
Compile one part to OpenSCAD.
Writes
.Pa part.scad
next to the input unless
.Fl o
is given.
.It Nm Cm stl Ar part.coscad Op Fl o Ar out.stl
Compile and render to an ASCII STL through OpenSCAD, then print the triangle
count, volume, and bounding box.
The intermediate
.Pa .scad
is kept beside the STL.
.It Nm Ar spec.assemble
Design stage.
Emits the assembled view
.Pq Pa spec_asm.scad ,
one print-oriented
.Pa spec_part_<variant>.scad
per unique (part, orientation), the packed plate(s)
.Pq Pa spec_plate.scad , or Pa spec_plate1.scad , Pa spec_plate2.scad ... ,
and
.Pa spec_manifest.json .
.It Nm Cm next Ar spec.assemble
Manufacturing stage.
Renders each variant once, chooses a print orientation where none was
declared (scoring bed contact, overhang, height, and slenderness on the real
mesh), packs instances largest-first across as many beds as needed, and
writes
.Pa spec_bed<N>.stl
plus a manifest recording per-variant orientation and per-instance
placements for slice-once, stamp-many slicing.
.It Nm Cm check Ar spec.assemble Op Fl -keep-temp
Interference and clearance check on real meshes.
Every part is rendered as placed by the
.Ql asm
expression; close pairs are intersected exactly by OpenSCAD.
Reports
.Ql OVERLAP
with its volume,
.Ql contact
for touching faces, and
.Ql WARN
for gaps below the declared
.Ql clearance .
Exit status 1 if any overlap.
Scratch renders go to the system temp directory and are removed unless
.Fl -keep-temp .
.It Nm Cm doctor
Report the OpenSCAD binary and BOSL2 checkout that will be used, their
versions, and the result of an end-to-end test render against a known
volume.
Exit status 1 if anything is missing.
.It Fl -version , Fl -help
Print the version, or the command list with a language cheat sheet.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width COSCAD_OPENSCAD
.It Ev COSCAD_OPENSCAD
The OpenSCAD binary, or a wrapper script such as
.Ql xvfb-run -a openscad "$@"
on a headless machine.
Otherwise
.Ql openscad
on
.Ev PATH
is used, then the usual install locations
.Pq the macOS app bundle, Program Files on Windows .
.It Ev COSCAD_BOSL2
A BOSL2 checkout outside the OpenSCAD library folders; its parent is
prepended to
.Ev OPENSCADPATH
when OpenSCAD runs.
Otherwise the library folders are searched
.Pq Pa ~/Documents/OpenSCAD/libraries , Pa ~/.local/share/OpenSCAD/libraries , ... .
.El
.Sh LANGUAGE
One definition per line,
.Ql name = expression .
Definitions resolve by dependency, not order.
Comments start with
.Ql // .
A line beginning with
.Ql |>
continues the previous definition.
The first code line may select a vocabulary:
.Ql !glyph
(glyph operators),
.Ql !simple
(ASCII words such as
.Ql Box ,
.Ql Translate.x ,
.Ql Hull ,
.Ql *
for union and
.Ql -
for difference), or neither, which accepts both.
.Ss Numbers
A definition whose right-hand side is arithmetic is a numeric binding.
Numbers may reference numbers, in any order, and are usable wherever a
number goes.
Argument positions take one atom
.Pq a literal, a name, Ql -name , or a parenthesized expression
so juxtaposed arguments stay unambiguous:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
w = 20
t = w / 5 - 1
main = box w (w / 2) t |> cutat top 0 0 (-t / 2) (zcyl 1 50)
.Ed
.Ss Shapes
.Bl -column "▬ x y z / box x y z" "description" -offset indent -compact
.It Sy syntax Ta Sy shape
.It ■ s Ta cube, corner at the origin (OpenSCAD)
.It ▬ x y z Ta box, corner at the origin
.It ● r Ta sphere
.It ◎ r h Ta cylinder, z from 0 to h
.It ▻ r h Ta cone
.It ⎏ n r h Ta n-sided prism
.It cube s / box x y z Ta centered cuboid (BOSL2)
.It sphere r / cyl r h Ta centered sphere, cylinder
.It xcyl r l / ycyl / zcyl Ta axis-aligned centered cylinders
.It tube or ir h Ta centered tube
.It torus R r Ta torus
.It wedge x y z Ta right-triangular prism, profile in the YZ plane
.It ▣ x y z c Ta cuboid, chamfer c
.It ◙ x y z r Ta cuboid, rounding r (< half the smallest dimension)
.It ⌭ r h c / ⌽ r h r2 Ta cylinder with chamfered / rounded ends
.It ⊚ or ir h Ta tube
.It ⏢ x1 y1 x2 y2 h Ta prismoid
.It ◉ R r Ta torus
.It ⊿ x y z Ta wedge
.El
.Ss 2D profiles
.Ql △ r ,
.Ql ⬠ r ,
.Ql ⭘ r
(triangle, pentagon, circle) and
.Ql ✎ x0 y0 x1 y1 ...
(a closed piecewise-cubic bezier outline, 3k+1 control points, evaluated by
the compiler).
Extrude with
.Ql ⮕ h profile
or
.Ql |> extrude h ;
offset with
.Ql profile ↯ ● r .
A profile used where a solid is expected, or the reverse, is a compile
error.
.Ss Lofts
.Ql loft z0 p0 z1 p1 ...
(glyph
.Ql ⟰ ,
.Ql Loft
in !simple) skins 2D profiles at ascending z into one solid through BOSL2
.Fn skin .
Profiles may differ in vertex count.
.Ql p0 |> loft z1 p1
starts a loft with
.Ql p0
at z = 0; further
.Ql |> loft z p
stages append.
Profiles must be single closed outlines: the 2D primitives, beziers, and
their in-plane transforms
.Pq χ ψ ω ⬈ ⇋ ↯ ;
booleans between profiles, ζ, θ, and ϕ are rejected.
.Ss Booleans
.Ql ⊕
union,
.Ql ⊖
difference (left minus right),
.Ql ∩
intersection,
.Ql ⇓
hull,
.Ql ⊞
minkowski.
Left-associative, one precedence level.
.Ss Transforms
.Ql χ ψ ζ d
translate along x/y/z;
.Ql θ ϕ ω deg
rotate about x/y/z (about the origin);
.Ql ⬈ sx sy sz
scale;
.Ql ⇋ nx ny nz
mirror;
.Ql ⚓ anchor
re-origin a shape at one of its own anchors.
A transform applies to the next primary expression; use parentheses or
.Ql $
.Pq Ql χ 5 $ a ⊕ b
for a compound argument.
.Ss Pipelines and anchors
.Ql a |> stage |> stage ...
applies postfix stages:
.Ql x y z d ,
.Ql move dx dy dz ,
.Ql rotx roty rotz deg ,
.Ql scale ,
.Ql mirror ,
.Ql extrude h ,
.Ql loft z p ,
.Ql anchor v ,
.Ql add cut isect hull mink shape ,
and the relational stages
.Ql at v [dx dy dz] child
(union; the child's opposite anchor meets anchor v),
.Ql on v [dx dy dz] child
(union; child rotated so +Z points along v, bottom mated there), and
.Ql cutat v [dx dy dz] cutter
(difference; the cutter is centered at the anchor).
Anchors are bounding-box points of the shape so far:
.Ql top bot lft rt fwd bak ctr ,
combinable as
.Ql top+rt
or
.Ql lft+fwd .
Glyph forms:
.Ql a ⌖ v b
positions,
.Ql a ⋈ v b
attaches.
.Sh ASSEMBLIES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
plate 250 250 6                      // bed width depth [margin]
clearance 0.15                       // minimum gap for `coscad check`
gap = 2                              // numbers work here too
center ← center.coscad ×1
larch  ← l_arch.coscad ×1 ▽top seam=rear
rail   ← rail.coscad ×0              // ×0: premade, assembly-only
corner ← corner.assemble ×2          // recursive subassembly
asm = center ⊕ (larch |> move (55 + gap) -13 -7) ⊕ rail
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql ▽anchor
declares which face goes on the bed; undeclared parts get the automatic
orientation search in
.Cm next .
.Ql key=value
entries are free hints carried into the manifest.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Cm check
exits 1 when any overlap is found,
.Cm doctor
when OpenSCAD, BOSL2, or the test render fails.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A bracket built relationally, then rendered:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
// bracket.coscad
plate  = box 5 15 20
flange = box 16 15 5
main = plate
  |> at top 5.5 0 -5 flange
  |> cutat lft 3.5 0 0 (xcyl 2.7 12)      // M5 clearance
  |> cutat top 2.5 0 -4 (zcyl 1.4 10)     // M3 pilot

$ coscad stl bracket.coscad
Wrote bracket.scad
Wrote bracket.stl: 664 triangles, volume 2638.931 mm^3, bounds ...
.Ed
.Pp
A funnel from numeric bindings and lofts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
r_top = 20
r_bot = 8
h = 40
wall = 2
outer = loft 0 (⭘ r_bot) h (⭘ r_top)
inner = loft -1 (⭘ (r_bot - wall)) (h + 1) (⭘ (r_top - wall))
main = outer ⊖ inner
.Ed
.Pp
Manufacture a three-part assembly and check its fits:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ coscad next bow3.assemble
Wrote bow3_bed1.stl (3 parts)
Wrote bow3_manifest.json
$ coscad check bow3.assemble
check: 3 parts, clearance = 0.0mm
contact  center x larch
contact  center x rarch
check: 0 overlaps, 0 clearance warnings
.Ed
.Pp
Verify the toolchain on a new machine:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ coscad doctor
OpenSCAD    ok       /opt/homebrew/bin/openscad (2025.05.16)
BOSL2       ok       /Users/me/Documents/OpenSCAD/libraries/BOSL2 (2.0.754)
round trip  ok       box 10 10 10 ⊖ zcyl 2 20 -> 874.67 mm^3 (expected 874.67)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Errors carry
.Ql file:line:col
and quote the offending line.
Distinguished cases: syntax errors, undefined names, circular dependencies
(only the cycle is listed), duplicate definitions, a number used as a shape
or a shape as a number, 2D/3D mismatches (extruding a solid, offsetting a
solid, combining a profile with a solid, a 2D
.Ql main ) ,
and invalid loft profiles.
OpenSCAD warnings during a render
.Pq a missing include, a dropped child
are treated as failures.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openscad 1
.Pp
